                        "entry_id": "89ddfc05-6038-390e-a9e2-058d1102c385",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Embellished with brocade."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d621a47-21fe-403f-875d-761b5e0e5ec7",
                                "sense_id": "a5168fc6-eba6-39e0-af88-84416a897cd1",
                                "text": "Brocaded Flow’rs o’er the gay Manteau shine,\nAnd the rich Stays her Taper Shape confine;\nThus all her Dress exerts a graceful Pride,\nAnd sporting Loves surround th’ expecting Bride […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6acfa46-71fb-4387-9cd4-0c0bc78f1c6f",
                                "sense_id": "a5168fc6-eba6-39e0-af88-84416a897cd1",
                                "text": "The next morning, after breakfast, the green maiden came to fetch Dorothy, and she dressed her in one of the prettiest gowns—made of green brocaded satin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "057fd053-d29a-43de-8bf4-e7bf5ff0daa1",
                                "sense_id": "a5168fc6-eba6-39e0-af88-84416a897cd1",
                                "text": "[…] slightly withdrawn behind these brocaded matrons sat a young girl in white with eyes ecstatically fixed on the stagelovers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50a04c6e-ef6a-442c-bce5-ed031b5f2aaf",
                                "sense_id": "a5168fc6-eba6-39e0-af88-84416a897cd1",
                                "text": "[…] she walked in the garden among brocaded moths, wearing a new gown of “powder-blue” chiffon […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba54a6a0-9993-40b0-8d23-4733ac6834a8",
                                "sense_id": "a5168fc6-eba6-39e0-af88-84416a897cd1",
                                "text": "Matsumoto Castle exhibits the architecture of both war and peace, from its steep wooden stairs, hidden inner levels and archer’s perches to the moon-viewing room added in 1630, which also offers a vantage point for viewing the brocaded carps and ducks residing in the castle moat."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
